---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import { LINKS } from '../consts';

// Terms of service. Paired with /privacy — Google's OAuth branding form asks for
// both, on the same host as the home page. Waffled is AGPL-3.0 software, not a
// hosted service, so these terms defer to the licence for the software itself and
// cover the website + the iOS app distribution.
const updated = 'September 1, 2026';
---

<Base
	title="Terms of service — Waffled"
	description="The terms that apply to the Waffled website, the Waffled iOS app, and the self-hosted Waffled software, which is licensed under the AGPL-3.0."
>
	<section class="legal">
		<div class="wrap">
			<div class="legal-head">
				<span class="eyebrow">Legal</span>
				<h1>Terms of service</h1>
				<p class="updated">Last updated {updated}</p>
			</div>

			<div class="legal-body">
				<div class="legal-callout">
					<p><strong>The short version.</strong> Waffled is free, open-source software you run yourself.
					We publish it; you host it. The software is covered by the AGPL-3.0 licence, it comes with no
					warranty, and because your installation is yours, you are responsible for how it is run and for
					the data in it.</p>
				</div>

				<h2>1. What these terms cover</h2>
				<p>These terms apply to the Waffled website (waffled.app and docs.waffled.app), the Waffled iOS
				app distributed through the App Store, and your use of the Waffled software. By using any of them
				you agree to these terms. If you do not agree, do not use them.</p>
				<p>We do not currently operate a hosted version of Waffled. If we offer one in the future, it will
				come with its own additional terms.</p>

				<h2>2. The software licence</h2>
				<p>The Waffled software is licensed under the
				<a href={LINKS.license} rel="noopener">GNU Affero General Public License v3.0</a>. That licence —
				not this page — governs your rights to use, modify and redistribute the source code, including the
				obligation to make your modifications available if you offer Waffled to others over a network.
				Where these terms and the AGPL-3.0 conflict on anything concerning the software itself, the
				licence wins.</p>

				<h2>3. Your installation is your responsibility</h2>
				<p>Waffled is self-hosted. When you install it you become the operator of that instance, which
				means you are responsible for:</p>
				<ul>
					<li>the server, network and storage it runs on, and the cost of them;</li>
					<li>securing it — HTTPS, strong credentials, keeping it updated, controlling who can reach
					it;</li>
					<li>backing up your data, and being able to restore it;</li>
					<li>the content your household puts into it, and complying with any laws that apply to you for
					handling that content — including data about children and any other people in your
					household.</li>
				</ul>
				<p>We have no access to your instance and cannot recover data, reset credentials, or restore
				backups for you.</p>

				<h2>4. Third-party services</h2>
				<p>Waffled can optionally connect to third-party services — Google Calendar, Microsoft Outlook
				calendar, Apple Health, Open Food Facts, and an AI model provider of your choosing. Those
				connections are yours: you authorise them, they are governed by that provider's own terms and
				privacy policy, and you must comply with those terms. We are not responsible for a third-party
				service changing, restricting or discontinuing its API. How Waffled handles data from these
				services is described in our <a href="/privacy">privacy policy</a>.</p>

				<h2>5. Acceptable use</h2>
				<p>Do not use the Waffled website or the iOS app to break the law, to attack or disrupt our
				infrastructure or anyone else's, or to gain unauthorised access to a Waffled instance you are not
				entitled to use. Do not represent modified versions of Waffled as being the official project.</p>

				<h2>6. Trademarks</h2>
				<p>The AGPL-3.0 grants you rights to the code; it does not grant rights to the Waffled name or
				logo. You may use them to refer to the project accurately. You may not use them in a way that
				suggests a modified or third-party version is the official Waffled, or that we endorse your
				product.</p>

				<h2>7. No warranty</h2>
				<p>Waffled, the website and the iOS app are provided <strong>"as is", without warranty of any
				kind</strong>, express or implied, including any warranty of merchantability, fitness for a
				particular purpose, or non-infringement. We do not warrant that the software will be
				uninterrupted, error-free, or that it will never lose data. This mirrors the disclaimer in the
				AGPL-3.0.</p>

				<h2>8. Limitation of liability</h2>
				<p>To the maximum extent permitted by law, the maintainers of Waffled are not liable for any
				indirect, incidental, special or consequential damages, or for any loss of data, profits or
				goodwill, arising out of your use of the software, the website or the app — even if we have been
				advised of the possibility. Some jurisdictions do not allow these exclusions, in which case they
				apply to you only as far as the law permits.</p>

				<h2>9. Changes</h2>
				<p>We may update these terms. Material changes will be reflected in the date at the top of this
				page. Continuing to use Waffled after a change means you accept the updated terms.</p>

				<h2>10. Contact</h2>
				<p>Questions about these terms can be raised as an issue at
				<a href={LINKS.issues} rel="noopener">github.com/kevinpsites/waffled/issues</a>.</p>
			</div>
		</div>
	</section>
</Base>
